title: Gryxa Toolkit Scheduled Task Persistence in Hidden Directories
id: a3f7c2e1-8b4d-4e9a-b6f2-1d5e8c3a7b90
status: experimental
description: >
  Detects creation of scheduled tasks pointing to executables in hidden or
  non-standard directories such as C:\ProgramData\WinRTCS or Windows Error
  Reporting-like paths, as used by the Gryxa toolkit for aggressive persistence.
  Gryxa creates at least seven scheduled tasks running as SYSTEM at 1/5/15 minute
  intervals across multiple hidden directories to survive incomplete remediation.
references:
  - https://gbhackers.com
  - https://cyberpress.org
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026-08-31
tags:
  - attack.t1053
  - attack.t1547
logsource:
  product: windows
  service: scheduled-task
detection:
  selection_hidden_dir:
    EventID: 106
    TaskName|contains:
      - '\WinRTCS\'
      - '\WerReporting\'
      - '\WinErr\'
      - '\ProgramData\.'
  selection_hidden_dir_action:
    EventID: 200
    TaskName|contains:
      - '\WinRTCS\'
      - '\WerReporting\'
      - '\WinErr\'
      - '\ProgramData\.'
  condition: selection_hidden_dir or selection_hidden_dir_action
falsepositives:
  - Legitimate software using ProgramData subdirectories for scheduled tasks
level: high
